{
  "summary": "The experiment tested replacing the RNA encoder (pca_n2000 → scvi_n200) in a multimodal multiprofile setup with avgpool aggregation and weighted fusion, achieving 67.8% validation accuracy (vs. 63.9% baseline) and 64.6% F1. This suggests the RNA encoder choice may be a critical factor, though uncertainty remains about whether other factors (e.g., interactions with image features) could also contribute. The result provides an initial indication but does not compare to alternative encoders, leaving the relative effectiveness of scvi_n200 uncertain."
}

